How we use them
Coral is for doing things. Primary buttons, an active tab, a selected filter, our logo mark. Please don't use it for big backgrounds, decorative shapes or paragraphs of text.
Text on coral is always white. No exceptions.
Ink, not black. We never use pure #000000 — Ink (#222222) is softer and easier on the eyes.
Slate is the lightest readable grey. If you're tempted to go lighter for "subtle" text, it probably won't pass contrast. Talk to us first.
Cards go on Mist. White cards on the grey canvas is what gives SpotStay its layered feel. A white card on a white background just disappears.
We don't have status colors yet. Success, warning and error aren't in the base CSS. If you're building a form or an alert, flag it with the design team so we can add proper tokens rather than everyone picking their own green.
A heads-up on contrast
We ran our main color pairs against WCAG 2.1:
