AA for large text only

The one to watch is our main button. White 16px text on #FF385C is a bit under the AA bar for regular-sized text. We're keeping it for now because it's core to how the brand looks, but if a project has strict accessibility requirements, use Deep Coral (#E61E4D) as the resting color instead. We'll revisit this as a team.
Typography
We keep type simple: one clean sans-serif, five sizes, three weights. Hierarchy should come from size and weight — if you find yourself reaching for a new color to make something stand out, try making it bolder or bigger first.
Our font
Right now the app uses each device's own system font, which keeps things fast and crisp everywhere. This is the stack we use:
font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
We've talked about licensing a brand typeface down the line. If we do, it'll be a rounded geometric sans (we've been looking at options like Inter and Nunito Sans) and it'll simply slot in at the front of this stack.
