One per row

Things to keep in mind on mobile
Anything tappable should be at least 44 × 44px. Our primary button is about 48px tall, so it's already fine.
Consider making the main button full width on mobile. It's much easier to hit with a thumb.
Before you hand off a design, check it at 360px, 768px, 1024px and 1440px. Most layout surprises show up at one of those.
Voice, accessibility & tokens
If SpotStay were a person, it'd be a good host: warm, helpful, and not overly chatty. Our words should sound like that too.
How we write
Here are a few real-world examples of the difference we're going for:
Sounds like SpotStay
Doesn't sound like SpotStay
"Add your first place to start welcoming guests."
"No data found. Click button to create entity."
"You're all set — your listing is live."
"Operation completed successfully."
"We couldn't save that. Try again in a moment."
"Error 500: request failed."

Talk to people as "you", and to SpotStay as "we".
Short sentences, everyday words. We say "place", "stay" and "guests", not "inventory" or "units".
Emoji are fine as empty-state illustrations, but please keep them out of buttons and headings.
Accessibility checklist
Run through this before handing anything off. It takes two minutes and saves a lot of rework.
Text meets the contrast ratios in the Color palette section.
Everything clickable has a visible focus style. Ours is outline: 2px solid #222222; outline-offset: 2px.
Buttons are actual <button> elements with labels that make sense on their own.
Property photos have useful alt text, like "Sunlit two-bedroom apartment in Indiranagar", not "image1.jpg".
Nothing relies on color alone to get its meaning across.
Our short list of do's and don'ts
Do save coral for the one thing that matters most on a screen.
Do let photos and numbers lead. The UI should stay out of the way.
Don't put borders or shadows on cards that are just sitting there.
Don't invent new colors, radii or spacing values. If the tokens below don't cover it, come and talk to us.
Don't borrow another company's logo, name or typeface. SpotStay takes cues from the best hospitality marketplaces, but it needs to look like itself.

